.TH FQ 1 "" "fq 0.1.0" "fleetq"
.SH NAME
fq \- Submit and manage jobs on the fleet queue (fleetqd on numpi)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fq
[\-\-json] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIoptions\fR] [\-\- \fIjob command\fR ...]
.SH COMMANDS
.SS "fq submit"
Submit a job.
.PP
.nf
fq submit [\-h] [\-\-json] [\-\-on ON] [\-\-each EACH] [\-\-allow\-clusters]
                 [\-\-queue QUEUE] [\-\-account ACCOUNT] [\-\-qos QOS]
                 [\-\-spill\-after SPILL_AFTER] [\-\-spill\-to SPILL_TO]
                 [\-\-gpus GPUS] [\-\-vram VRAM] [\-\-gpu\-model GPU_MODEL]
                 [\-\-cpus CPUS] [\-\-mem MEM] [\-\-time TIME] [\-\-scratch SCRATCH]
                 [\-\-dir DIR] [\-\-in\-place IN_PLACE] [\-\-exclude EXCLUDE]
                 [\-\-needs NEEDS] [\-\-needs\-rw NEEDS_RW] [\-\-env ENV]
                 [\-\-env\-file ENV_FILE] [\-\-setup SETUP] [\-\-after AFTER]
                 [\-\-array ARRAY] [\-\-priority PRIORITY] [\-\-name NAME] [\-\-hold]
                 [\-\-begin BEGIN] [\-\-retry RETRY] [\-\-retry\-on RETRY_ON]
                 [\-\-warn\-signal WARN_SIGNAL] [\-\-warn\-before WARN_BEFORE]
                 [\-\-resume N] [\-\-kill\-grace KILL_GRACE] [\-\-collect COLLECT]
                 [\-\-idempotency\-key IDEMPOTENCY_KEY] [\-\-wait]
                 [\-\-timeout TIMEOUT] [\-\-propagate\-exit] [\-\-dry\-run]
                 [\-\-wrap WRAP] [\-\-script SCRIPT]
                 [\-\-script\-args [SCRIPT_ARGS ...]]
                 [argv ...]
.fi
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
print exactly one JSON object on stdout
.TP
\fB\-\-on\fR \fION\fR
run once on any one of these destinations (a,b)
.TP
\fB\-\-each\fR \fIEACH\fR
run one job per destination (a,b)
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-clusters\fR
let fleetq place it on a Slurm site without naming one (needs a token that allows it)
.TP
\fB\-\-queue\fR \fIQUEUE\fR
cluster queue, e.g. kiac:a100
.TP
\fB\-\-account\fR \fIACCOUNT\fR
Slurm account on the cluster
.TP
\fB\-\-qos\fR \fIQOS\fR
Slurm QOS on the cluster
.TP
\fB\-\-spill\-after\fR \fISPILL_AFTER\fR
if not started within this long (e.g. 2h), also try \-\-spill\-to
.TP
\fB\-\-spill\-to\fR \fISPILL_TO\fR
destinations to spill to, e.g. kiac:a100,amd
.TP
\fB\-\-gpus\fR \fIGPUS\fR
whole GPUs (required; 0 for CPU\-only)
.TP
\fB\-\-vram\fR \fIVRAM\fR
minimum VRAM per GPU, e.g. 24G
.TP
\fB\-\-gpu\-model\fR \fIGPU_MODEL\fR
only this GPU model, as `fq nodes` names it
.TP
\fB\-\-cpus\fR \fICPUS\fR
CPU cores
.TP
\fB\-\-mem\fR \fIMEM\fR
total RAM, e.g. 32G
.TP
\fB\-\-time\fR \fITIME\fR
walltime, e.g. 4h or 1\-00:00:00
.TP
\fB\-\-scratch\fR \fISCRATCH\fR
writable scratch space, e.g. 50G
.TP
\fB\-\-dir\fR \fIDIR\fR
directory to snapshot and upload (default: .)
.TP
\fB\-\-in\-place\fR \fIIN_PLACE\fR
run code already at this path on the node (needs \-\-on/\-\-each)
.TP
\fB\-\-exclude\fR \fIEXCLUDE\fR
leave this pattern out of the uploaded snapshot (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-needs\fR \fINEEDS\fR
a path that must be readable on the node
.TP
\fB\-\-needs\-rw\fR \fINEEDS_RW\fR
a path that must be writable on the node
.TP
\fB\-\-env\fR \fIENV\fR
KEY=VALUE (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-env\-file\fR \fIENV_FILE\fR
KEY=VALUE lines (never sourced as shell); wins over \-\-env
.TP
\fB\-\-setup\fR \fISETUP\fR
shell run before the command (e.g. activate a venv)
.TP
\fB\-\-after\fR \fIAFTER\fR
[afterok|afterany|afternotok|after:]JOBID or GROUP (grp_...); repeatable
.TP
\fB\-\-array\fR \fIARRAY\fR
indices, e.g. 0\-9%2 (at most 2 at once); each task reads $FQ_ARRAY_TASK_ID
.TP
\fB\-\-priority\fR \fIPRIORITY\fR
\-1000..1000, higher is placed sooner (default 0); waiting jobs also gain priority as they age
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fINAME\fR
job name (default: the command's basename)
.TP
\fB\-\-hold\fR
queue it held; start it later with `fq release`
.TP
\fB\-\-begin\fR \fIBEGIN\fR
not before this time: +2h, or local 2026\-09\-24T09:00
.TP
\fB\-\-retry\fR \fIRETRY\fR
rerun up to N times on the \-\-retry\-on causes
.TP
\fB\-\-retry\-on\fR \fIRETRY_ON\fR
node_fail,exit,timeout,oom,preempted
.TP
\fB\-\-warn\-signal\fR \fIWARN_SIGNAL\fR
signal the job this long before its walltime: USR1, USR2, INT, HUP
.TP
\fB\-\-warn\-before\fR \fIWARN_BEFORE\fR
how long before the walltime to signal (default 5m)
.TP
\fB\-\-resume\fR \fIN\fR
checkpointing job: warn with USR1 before walltime and resubmit up to N times after timeout/preemption/node failure, back on the machine holding $FQ_CHECKPOINT_DIR
.TP
\fB\-\-kill\-grace\fR \fIKILL_GRACE\fR
time between SIGTERM and SIGKILL on cancel (default 60s)
.TP
\fB\-\-collect\fR \fICOLLECT\fR
relative output path to bring back for `fq fetch`
.TP
\fB\-\-idempotency\-key\fR \fIIDEMPOTENCY_KEY\fR
stable key for this exact request (derive it from the task); a retry with the same key returns the original job instead of a second one
.TP
\fB\-\-wait\fR
block until the job ends (prints its id first)
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fITIMEOUT\fR
with \-\-wait: stop waiting after this long (exit 4; the job keeps running)
.TP
\fB\-\-propagate\-exit\fR
with \-\-wait on one job: exit with the job's own exit code (which can collide with 2\-8)
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
print the job spec and the upload; submit nothing
.TP
\fB\-\-wrap\fR \fIWRAP\fR
a shell command line, run with bash \-c
.TP
\fB\-\-script\fR \fISCRIPT\fR
a script inside the uploaded snapshot, by relative path
.TP
\fB\-\-script\-args\fR \fISCRIPT_ARGS\fR
arguments for \-\-script
.TP
\fIargv\fR
the command; put it after `\-\-`
.PP
.nf
The command goes last, after `\-\-`:  fq submit \-\-gpus 1 \-\- python train.py \-\-lr 3e\-4
or use \-\-wrap 'CMD' (run by bash \-c) or \-\-script PATH (a file in the snapshot).

By default the current directory is snapshotted and uploaded (\-\-dir, \-\-exclude);
\-\-in\-place runs code that already sits at a path on the chosen machine instead.
Use \-\-dry\-run first to see the spec, and the upload, without submitting.
.fi
.SS "fq wait"
Wait for jobs to finish.
.PP
.nf
fq wait [\-h] [\-\-json] [\-\-timeout TIMEOUT] [\-\-propagate\-exit]
               jobs [jobs ...]
.fi
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
print exactly one JSON object on stdout
.TP
\fIjobs\fR
job ids
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fITIMEOUT\fR
stop waiting after this long (exit 4; the jobs keep running)
.TP
\fB\-\-propagate\-exit\fR
with one job: exit with the job's exit code
.SS "fq queue (q)"
Squeue: running and waiting jobs, in dispatch order.
.PP
.nf
fq queue [\-h] [\-\-json] [\-\-all] [\-u USER] [\-\-all\-users] [\-t STATE]
                [\-n NAME] [\-w WHERE] [\-\-group GROUP] [\-o FORMAT] [\-\-noheader]
                [\-\-watch [SECONDS]] [\-\-limit LIMIT]
.fi
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
print exactly one JSON object on stdout
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
include finished jobs
.TP
\fB\-u\fR, \fB\-\-user\fR \fIUSER\fR
another user's jobs (needs manage_all)
.TP
\fB\-\-all\-users\fR
everyone's jobs (needs manage_all)
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-state\fR \fISTATE\fR
e.g. PD,R or PENDING,RUNNING
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-name\fR \fINAME\fR
glob on the job name, e.g. 'sweep\-*'
.TP
\fB\-w\fR, \fB\-\-where\fR \fIWHERE\fR
only jobs placed on this machine or cluster
.TP
\fB\-\-group\fR \fIGROUP\fR
members of one array or \-\-each group
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fIFORMAT\fR
columns, default id,name,user,st,where,gpus,time,limit,prio,pos,reason
.TP
\fB\-\-noheader\fR
no column header
.TP
\fB\-\-watch\fR \fISECONDS\fR
redraw every N s (at least 2; default 5); not with \-\-json
.TP
\fB\-\-limit\fR \fILIMIT\fR
at most this many rows (default 500)
.SS "fq history (sacct)"
Sacct: finished jobs with wait, run time and GPU\-hours.
.PP
.nf
fq history [\-h] [\-\-json] [\-\-since SINCE] [\-\-summary] [\-u USER]
                  [\-\-all\-users] [\-w WHERE] [\-o FORMAT] [\-\-limit LIMIT]
.fi
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
print exactly one JSON object on stdout
.TP
\fB\-\-since\fR \fISINCE\fR
how far back, e.g. 24h, 30d (default 7d)
.TP
\fB\-\-summary\fR
totals per machine
.TP
\fB\-u\fR, \fB\-\-user\fR \fIUSER\fR
another user's jobs (needs manage_all)
.TP
\fB\-\-all\-users\fR
everyone's jobs (needs manage_all)
.TP
\fB\-w\fR, \fB\-\-where\fR \fIWHERE\fR
only jobs that ran on this machine or cluster
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fIFORMAT\fR
columns, default id,name,st,where,gpus,wait,time,gpuh,outcome,reason
.TP
\fB\-\-limit\fR \fILIMIT\fR
at most this many rows (default 1000)
.SS "fq show"
One job's full record, as JSON.
.PP
.nf
fq show [\-h] [\-\-json] job
.fi
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
print exactly one JSON object on stdout
.TP
\fIjob\fR
job id
.SS "fq explain"
Why a job is waiting, or where it was placed.
.PP
.nf
fq explain [\-h] [\-\-json] job
.fi
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
print exactly one JSON object on stdout
.TP
\fIjob\fR
job id
.SS "fq cancel"
Cancel jobs by id, or every unfinished job matching the filters.
.PP
.nf
fq cancel [\-h] [\-\-json] [\-\-name NAME] [\-\-group GROUP] [\-\-phase PHASE]
                 [jobs ...]
.fi
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
print exactly one JSON object on stdout
.TP
\fIjobs\fR
job ids
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fINAME\fR
glob on the job name, e.g. 'sweep\-*'
.TP
\fB\-\-group\fR \fIGROUP\fR
every member of an \-\-each group or array (grp_...)
.TP
\fB\-\-phase\fR \fIPHASE\fR
only jobs in this phase, e.g. PENDING
.SS "fq hold"
Hold jobs by id, or every unfinished job matching the filters.
.PP
.nf
fq hold [\-h] [\-\-json] [\-\-name NAME] [\-\-group GROUP] [\-\-phase PHASE]
               [jobs ...]
.fi
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
print exactly one JSON object on stdout
.TP
\fIjobs\fR
job ids
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fINAME\fR
glob on the job name, e.g. 'sweep\-*'
.TP
\fB\-\-group\fR \fIGROUP\fR
every member of an \-\-each group or array (grp_...)
.TP
\fB\-\-phase\fR \fIPHASE\fR
only jobs in this phase, e.g. PENDING
.SS "fq release"
Release jobs by id, or every unfinished job matching the filters.
.PP
.nf
fq release [\-h] [\-\-json] [\-\-name NAME] [\-\-group GROUP] [\-\-phase PHASE]
                  [jobs ...]
.fi
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
print exactly one JSON object on stdout
.TP
\fIjobs\fR
job ids
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fINAME\fR
glob on the job name, e.g. 'sweep\-*'
.TP
\fB\-\-group\fR \fIGROUP\fR
every member of an \-\-each group or array (grp_...)
.TP
\fB\-\-phase\fR \fIPHASE\fR
only jobs in this phase, e.g. PENDING
.SS "fq top"
Move a job ahead of your other waiting jobs.
.PP
.nf
fq top [\-h] [\-\-json] job
.fi
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
print exactly one JSON object on stdout
.TP
\fIjob\fR
job id
.SS "fq requeue"
Run a finished job again, as a new job.
.PP
.nf
fq requeue [\-h] [\-\-json] job
.fi
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
print exactly one JSON object on stdout
.TP
\fIjob\fR
job id
.SS "fq modify"
Change a job that has not started (what it runs cannot change).
.PP
.nf
fq modify [\-h] [\-\-json] [\-\-vram VRAM] [\-\-gpu\-model GPU_MODEL]
                 [\-\-mem MEM] [\-\-time TIME] [\-\-scratch SCRATCH] [\-\-on ON]
                 [\-\-queue QUEUE] [\-\-account ACCOUNT] [\-\-qos QOS]
                 [\-\-begin BEGIN] [\-\-name NAME] [\-\-gpus GPUS] [\-\-cpus CPUS]
                 [\-\-priority PRIORITY] [\-\-retry RETRY] [\-\-allow\-clusters]
                 [\-\-begin\-now]
                 job
.fi
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
print exactly one JSON object on stdout
.TP
\fIjob\fR
job id
.TP
\fB\-\-vram\fR \fIVRAM\fR
minimum VRAM per GPU, e.g. 24G
.TP
\fB\-\-gpu\-model\fR \fIGPU_MODEL\fR
only this GPU model
.TP
\fB\-\-mem\fR \fIMEM\fR
total RAM, e.g. 32G
.TP
\fB\-\-time\fR \fITIME\fR
walltime, e.g. 4h
.TP
\fB\-\-scratch\fR \fISCRATCH\fR
scratch space, e.g. 50G
.TP
\fB\-\-on\fR \fION\fR
destinations (a,b)
.TP
\fB\-\-queue\fR \fIQUEUE\fR
cluster queue, e.g. kiac:a100
.TP
\fB\-\-account\fR \fIACCOUNT\fR
Slurm account
.TP
\fB\-\-qos\fR \fIQOS\fR
Slurm QOS
.TP
\fB\-\-begin\fR \fIBEGIN\fR
not before: +2h or 2026\-09\-24T09:00
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fINAME\fR
job name
.TP
\fB\-\-gpus\fR \fIGPUS\fR
whole GPUs
.TP
\fB\-\-cpus\fR \fICPUS\fR
CPU cores
.TP
\fB\-\-priority\fR \fIPRIORITY\fR
\-1000..1000, higher is placed sooner
.TP
\fB\-\-retry\fR \fIRETRY\fR
reruns allowed
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-clusters\fR
let it be placed on a Slurm site
.TP
\fB\-\-begin\-now\fR
drop a \-\-begin time (wins over \-\-begin)
.SS "fq priority"
Set a waiting job's priority.
.PP
.nf
fq priority [\-h] [\-\-json] job value
.fi
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
print exactly one JSON object on stdout
.TP
\fIjob\fR
job id
.TP
\fIvalue\fR
new priority, \-1000..1000; higher is placed sooner
.SS "fq shell"
A shell (or `\-\- CMD`) inside a running workstation job.
.PP
.nf
fq shell [\-h] [\-\-json] job
.fi
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
print exactly one JSON object on stdout
.TP
\fIjob\fR
job id
.SS "fq alloc (salloc)"
Hold idle GPUs on a workstation for interactive work.
.PP
.nf
fq alloc [\-h] [\-\-json] [\-\-gpus GPUS] [\-\-time TIME] [\-\-on ON]
                [\-\-mem MEM] [\-\-vram VRAM] [\-\-gpu\-model GPU_MODEL]
                [\-\-in\-place IN_PLACE] [\-\-dir DIR]
                [\-\-idempotency\-key IDEMPOTENCY_KEY] [\-\-cpus CPUS]
                [\-\-priority PRIORITY] [\-\-name NAME] [\-\-timeout TIMEOUT]
                [\-\-shell] [\-\-keep]
.fi
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
print exactly one JSON object on stdout
.TP
\fB\-\-gpus\fR \fIGPUS\fR
whole GPUs (default 1)
.TP
\fB\-\-time\fR \fITIME\fR
how long to hold them (default 2h)
.TP
\fB\-\-on\fR \fION\fR
any one of these workstations
.TP
\fB\-\-mem\fR \fIMEM\fR
total RAM, e.g. 32G
.TP
\fB\-\-vram\fR \fIVRAM\fR
minimum VRAM per GPU, e.g. 24G
.TP
\fB\-\-gpu\-model\fR \fIGPU_MODEL\fR
only this GPU model
.TP
\fB\-\-in\-place\fR \fIIN_PLACE\fR
work in code already at this path
.TP
\fB\-\-dir\fR \fIDIR\fR
directory to snapshot and upload (default: .)
.TP
\fB\-\-idempotency\-key\fR \fIIDEMPOTENCY_KEY\fR
stable key: a retry returns the same allocation
.TP
\fB\-\-cpus\fR \fICPUS\fR
CPU cores
.TP
\fB\-\-priority\fR \fIPRIORITY\fR
\-1000..1000, higher is placed sooner
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fINAME\fR
job name (default alloc)
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fITIMEOUT\fR
give up waiting for GPUs after this long (job stays queued)
.TP
\fB\-\-shell\fR
open a shell at once; release the GPUs when it exits
.TP
\fB\-\-keep\fR
with \-\-shell: keep the allocation after the shell exits
.SS "fq logs"
Print a job's output from the numpi log cache.
.PP
.nf
fq logs [\-h] [\-\-json] [\-\-err] [\-\-tail BYTES] [\-\-offset OFFSET]
               [\-\-attempt ATTEMPT] [\-\-follow] [\-\-raw]
               job
.fi
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
print exactly one JSON object on stdout
.TP
\fIjob\fR
job id
.TP
\fB\-\-err\fR
stderr instead of stdout
.TP
\fB\-\-tail\fR \fIBYTES\fR
only the last BYTES (ignored with \-\-offset)
.TP
\fB\-\-offset\fR \fIOFFSET\fR
start at this byte offset
.TP
\fB\-\-attempt\fR \fIATTEMPT\fR
an earlier attempt of a retried job
.TP
\fB\-\-follow\fR, \fB\-f\fR
keep reading until the log is complete
.TP
\fB\-\-raw\fR
write exact stored bytes instead of cleaning captured terminal progress output
.SS "fq fetch"
Download a job's collected outputs (\-\-collect), checking each hash.
.PP
.nf
fq fetch [\-h] [\-\-json] [\-o OUTPUT] [\-\-overwrite] [\-\-attempt ATTEMPT]
                job [paths ...]
.fi
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
print exactly one JSON object on stdout
.TP
\fIjob\fR
job id
.TP
\fIpaths\fR
only these relative paths (default: all)
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fIOUTPUT\fR
directory to write into (default: .)
.TP
\fB\-\-overwrite\fR
replace existing destination files
.TP
\fB\-\-attempt\fR \fIATTEMPT\fR
an earlier attempt of a retried job
.SS "fq nodes"
Fleetq's machines: state, drain, and the GPUs it has reserved.
.PP
.nf
fq nodes [\-h] [\-\-json]
.fi
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
print exactly one JSON object on stdout
.SS "fq usage"
Measured GPU, CPU and memory use, and which GPUs are idle (cached).
.PP
.nf
fq usage [\-h] [\-\-json] [\-\-idle] [machine]
.fi
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
print exactly one JSON object on stdout
.TP
\fImachine\fR
one Fleetmon machine (default: all)
.TP
\fB\-\-idle\fR
only GPUs Fleetmon proves idle (two fresh idle samples)
.SS "fq admin"
Pause dispatch or stop new admission while preserving cancellation.
.PP
.nf
fq admin [\-h] [\-\-json] {pause,resume,accept\-off,accept\-on}
.fi
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
print exactly one JSON object on stdout
.TP
\fIoperation\fR {pause,resume,accept-off,accept-on}
pause/resume dispatch, or stop/start accepting new jobs
.SS "fq node"
Drain or resume one node.
.PP
.nf
fq node [\-h] [\-\-json] [\-\-reason REASON] {drain,resume} name
.fi
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
print exactly one JSON object on stdout
.TP
\fIoperation\fR {drain,resume}
stop placing work there, or start again
.TP
\fIname\fR
node id, as `fq nodes` lists it
.TP
\fB\-\-reason\fR \fIREASON\fR
reason recorded with a drain
.SS "fq whoami"
The token's owner, kind and scopes.
.PP
.nf
fq whoami [\-h] [\-\-json]
.fi
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
print exactly one JSON object on stdout
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.nf
  0  ok (wait: the job succeeded)        5  fleetqd unreachable: retry, same \-\-idempotency\-key
  1  the job ended unsuccessfully        6  authentication (token missing, revoked, unreadable)
  2  refused or usage error: the answer  7  server or version error
  3  not found                           8  rate limited
  4  wait timed out; the job runs on   130  interrupted; any submitted job runs on
.fi
.SH "ENVIRONMENT"
.nf
  FQ_URL         fleetqd origin, HTTPS (plain HTTP only on 127.0.0.1 or ::1)
  FQ_TOKEN_FILE  token file, mode 0600 (default ~/.config/fleetq/token)
  FQ_CONFIG      client config with `url` and `token_file` (default ~/.config/fleetq/client.toml)
  FQ_FLEETCTL    fleetctl used by `fq shell`
.fi
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.nf
  fq usage \-\-idle                                  GPUs free right now (cached; contacts no machine)
  fq \-\-json submit \-\-idempotency\-key exp1\-seed0 \-\-gpus 1 \-\-on rtx4090 \-\- python train.py \-\-seed 0
  fq submit \-\-gpus 1 \-\-array 0\-9%4 \-\-name sweep \-\- python train.py   (task id in $FQ_ARRAY_TASK_ID)
  fq \-\-json wait 42 \-\-timeout 9m                   exit 4 means still running: call it again
  fq logs 42 \-\-tail 4000 ; fq explain 42 ; fq cancel \-\-name 'sweep*'
.fi
.SH NOTES
\-\-json may go before or after the subcommand. Everything after a bare `\-\-` is
the job's command, passed through untouched. Reads (q, history, usage, nodes,
logs) come from numpi's caches and never contact a machine, so they are safe
to repeat: use them, not squeue, sacct or nvidia\-smi over ssh, for fleetq jobs
and Fleetmon\-monitored machines. (They do not see other users' Slurm jobs.)
.SH SEE ALSO
fleetctl help, fleetqd(1) \- the daemon's own --help, fleetq/README.md
